<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">30042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The Pentagon's put the first official price tag on America's war with Iran at twenty-five billion dollars, and Defense Secretary Hegseth's refused to give Congress a timeline or an end-state.</s> <s>Sixty days into a conflict no Congress has authorised, he called the lawmakers asking those questions reckless, feckless and defeatist.</s> <s>The War Powers deadline arrives Friday with no plan in place to meet it.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>New Zealand's Court of Appeal has rejected Brenton Tarrant's bid to withdraw his guilty pleas for the twenty-nineteen Christchurch mosque attacks that killed fifty-one Muslim worshippers.</s> <s>Judges dismissed his claims of mental illness after prison staff and medical records contradicted them, and his appeal arrived five hundred and five days late.</s> <s>Tarrant will serve out life without parole, sparing the victims' families a retrial that would have handed him a courtroom stage.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>President Trump's confirmed a review of the thirty-six thousand US troops stationed in Germany, with Ramstein Air Base — <sub alias="NATO">NATO</sub>'s main logistics hub for Ukraine and the Middle East — sitting at the centre of any drawdown.</s> <s>Berlin released its first national military strategy just last week, a quiet admission that Europe's preparing to defend itself without Washington.</s> <s>Trump said the decision will come in a short period, language that's worried capitals from Warsaw to Paris.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli forces are bolting wire mesh onto Merkava tanks in southern Lebanon, an improvised defence after Hezbollah's fibre-optic drones killed one Israeli soldier and wounded six others on Sunday.</s> <s>The fibre tether defeats electronic jamming, leaving a five-hundred-dollar quadcopter able to disable a seven-million-dollar tank.</s> <s>It's the same lesson Russian armour learned in Ukraine, now playing out three months into a ceasefire that hasn't stopped daily strikes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Manhattan prosecutors have indicted a sitting Mexican governor on cartel-conspiracy charges, accusing Sinaloa's Rubén Rocha Moya of trading drug-route protection for the kidnapping of political rivals during his election.</s> <s>It's one of the highest-ranking foreign officials ever charged by US courts with cartel conspiracy.</s> <s>Mexico's foreign ministry's rejected the indictment as evidentially baseless and warned Washington against weaponising prosecution as a tool of sovereignty pressure.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>President Putin offered to take Iran's enriched uranium off Tehran's hands during a ninety-minute call with Trump, then warned of extremely harmful consequences if Washington and Israel resume strikes.</s> <s>Moscow's positioning itself as broker and deterrent in the same conversation, the indispensable backchannel European powers no longer hold.</s> <s>Putin also floated a new Ukraine framework, a reminder that any Iran settlement now runs through the Kremlin.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Rats now infest eighty percent of Gaza's tent settlements, exposing one and a half million displaced people to rodent-borne disease, with more than seventy thousand skin infections recorded this year alone.</s> <s>Destroyed sanitation, uncleared rubble, and Israel's continuing blockade on repair materials are the documented mechanism.</s> <s>Gaza City's health chief said his people are fighting two wars now — the war of bombs and the war of rats.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Syria's transitional government's arrested Amjad Youssef in rural Hama, the man filmed executing forty-one civilians in the Tadamon massacre for Assad's intelligence branch in twenty-thirteen.</s> <s>He'd evaded capture for thirteen years after burning the bodies in a pit he'd dug himself.</s> <s>Damascus says dozens of similar warrants remain open as the country begins its long reckoning with the regime that killed it.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Canada's made the Arctic port of Churchill a federal priority, betting on climate-driven sea-ice retreat to extend a shipping window that today runs only four to five months a year.</s> <s>Prime Minister Carney sees Churchill as a sovereignty asset against US tariff pressure and a route to double non-American exports within a decade.</s> <s>No construction timeline exists, and unresolved Cree and Inuit consent questions still shadow the plan.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's draft motor vehicle rules will legitimise ethanol blends up to one hundred percent alongside pure biodiesel — opening a regulatory door for flex-fuel vehicles that until now had no path to certification.</s> <s>Toyota and other automakers say they're ready to launch as soon as the rules clear thirty days of public comment.</s> <s>The bet implies roughly fifteen billion dollars in import savings, but ties Indian fuel policy directly to sugarcane harvests and Bihar farm economics.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United Arab Emirates is preparing to leave OPEC after fifty years, frustrated that Saudi-led quotas cap its output at a fraction of nameplate capacity while Iran-war disruption squeezes Gulf revenue.</s> <s>Abu Dhabi wants four million barrels a day; the cartel allots roughly three point two.</s> <s>The exit splits the Gulf at the worst possible moment for Riyadh, and reshapes how Tehran reads its neighbours across the water.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Gulf sukuk issuance hit fifty-five billion dollars in the first quarter, a record, with Saudi Arabia leading the funding round to keep Vision Twenty-Thirty capital projects moving as Iran-war oil prices compress state revenue.</s> <s>Sharia-compliant funds across the Gulf and Asia absorbed the supply without difficulty.</s> <s>Riyadh's officials say further issuance will follow, a quiet sign that the kingdom now finances its ambitions through debt rather than crude.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A decade of popular-science orthodoxy is now under formal dispute, as ecologists challenge Suzanne Simard's foundational claim that trees exchange nutrients through underground fungal networks.</s> <s>Her mycorrhizal data, the basis for what readers came to call the Wood Wide Web, no longer holds up cleanly under independent reanalysis.</s> <s>Simard's new book defends the framework — but whether the evidence does is a different question entirely.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A long-derided philosophy of mathematics is producing real results — ultrafinitism, the view that numbers larger than any feasible computation simply do not exist.</s> <s>Doron Zeilberger and a small group of working mathematicians argue infinity is a useful fiction the universe never instantiates, a position quantum-gravity researchers borrow whenever they try to make spacetime discrete.</s> <s>Whether physics can rebuild itself on finite foundations remains genuinely open.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Disaster forecasters can't yet trust artificial intelligence in extreme weather, a new Science Advances paper warns.</s> <s>Models trained on the historical record systematically miss unprecedented events — exactly the conditions a warming climate is already producing.</s> <s>The authors called it a warning shot against the rush to replace traditional numerical forecasting, the kind of system that still has to flag the floods nobody's seen before.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Google's announced that every Android app — including those installed by sideloading — must come from a developer who's registered with Google, paid a fee, and submitted government identification.</s> <s>F-Droid, the leading catalogue of open-source apps, has called the mandate existential.</s> <s>The change retroactively converts three billion phones into a curated walled garden, just as the European Union's Digital Markets Act tries to push Android in the opposite direction.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Zambia's cancelled the RightsCon human rights conference days before it was due to open in Lusaka, citing pending security clearances for unnamed speakers.</s> <s>Activists whose own governments had flagged them were effectively barred, and organisers told thousands of registered attendees to cancel their travel.</s> <s>No new venue or date exists for what's grown into the world's largest digital rights gathering.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Alibaba has cut thirty-four percent of its workforce and Baidu seven percent — not from weakness, but to fund the same artificial intelligence pivot American tech giants made openly.</s> <s>China's platforms are quietly rebuilding around model teams without public earnings disclosures.</s> <s>Chinese workers have no US-style severance to soften the transition; they're absorbing the industry's restructuring on their own.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>